\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Reading Tracker \'97 UI/UX Visual Design Review\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Executive Summary\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 The current interface has a strong foundation: the dark background, starfield, minimal navigation, and sidebar create a distinctive atmosphere for a reading-focused application. However, the window chrome, surface hierarchy, and background bubble/glow treatment currently compete with the application itself.\
The biggest issue is visual cohesion. The app feels like a dark interface placed inside a generic macOS window rather than one intentionally designed, unified surface. The title-bar area carries too much visual weight, while the bubble/glow effect introduces additional boundaries that don't consistently align with the actual UI geometry.\
The overall goal should be to make the surrounding chrome recede and allow the reading interface to become the dominant visual surface.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 1. Window Chrome Is Visually Dominating the Interface\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Problem\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 The large gray title-bar area creates a strong horizontal separation between the macOS window frame and the application content.\
Instead of feeling like part of the application, the title bar reads as a separate surface sitting above it. This creates a visual hierarchy where the window frame competes with the actual application UI.\
The result is that the interface feels more like:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Generic macOS window \uc0\u8594  application underneath\cf2 \strokec3 \
rather than:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 One cohesive Reading Tracker interface\cf2 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 UX/UI Impact\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Reduces visual cohesion.\
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Makes the application feel less polished and intentional.\
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Creates an unnecessary visual interruption at the top of the screen.\
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Draws attention away from the sidebar and main content.\
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Makes the app feel more like a webpage or embedded interface inside a native window.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Recommendation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 The window chrome should become substantially more visually integrated with the application.\
Consider:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Matching the title-bar background more closely to the application's background.\
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Reducing the contrast between the title bar and content.\
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Allowing the app surface to visually extend into the title-bar region where appropriate.\
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Minimizing unnecessary borders and horizontal separators.\
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Treating the macOS chrome as something that should recede into the interface rather than announce itself.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 The guiding principle should be:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 The chrome should support the application, not compete with it.\cf2 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 2. The Interface Has Too Many Competing Visual Surfaces\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 There are currently several distinct layers competing for attention:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 macOS window chrome\
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 application background\
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 sidebar surface\
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 main content surface\
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 bubble/glow effect\
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 starfield\
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 individual UI elements\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Individually these elements can work, but together they create a sense of visual fragmentation.\
The interface needs a clearer surface hierarchy so that the user immediately understands what is the application, what is navigation, and what is merely atmospheric decoration.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Recommendation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Reduce the number of visually independent surfaces.\
The background treatment should primarily establish atmosphere, while the actual application surfaces should establish structure.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 3. Bubble/Glow Effect Is Misaligned With the UI Geometry\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Problem\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 The bubble/glow effect does not feel sufficiently anchored to the actual geometry of the application.\
Its boundaries and curvature don't consistently correspond to the edges of the sidebar, main content area, or window itself. This makes the effect feel like an independent layer floating behind the interface.\
Instead of reinforcing the structure of the UI, it introduces another set of visual boundaries.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 UX/UI Impact\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 This creates a subtle but persistent feeling that something is "off" even though the individual elements appear aesthetically pleasing.\
The user may not consciously identify the problem as alignment, but the composition feels less intentional because:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 The glow doesn't consistently follow the window geometry.\
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Its curvature doesn't clearly relate to the content boundaries.\
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 The visual center of the effect doesn't necessarily correspond to the visual center of the application.\
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 The background decoration appears to exist on a different coordinate system than the UI.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Recommendation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 The bubble/glow should be treated as part of the application's layout rather than an independent decorative element.\
It should either:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Align precisely with the application/window geometry, or\
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Be made sufficiently diffuse/subtle that its exact boundaries no longer matter.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 The current middle ground makes the misalignment particularly noticeable.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 4. The Background Effect Creates Competing Boundaries\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 The bubble treatment is currently strong enough that the eye interprets it as another physical surface.\
This is problematic because the application already has clear structural boundaries between:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Sidebar\
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Main content\
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Window\
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Title bar\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Adding another large curved boundary creates unnecessary complexity.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Recommendation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Choose one visual language:\
Structured UI\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Clean rectangular/rounded surfaces\
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Clear alignment\
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Strong grid\
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Minimal background geometry\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Atmospheric UI\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Soft gradients\
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Diffuse glows\
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Starfield\
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Little or no visible boundary\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 The current design is attempting to do both simultaneously.\
A more successful implementation would make the bubble effect support the atmospheric aesthetic without becoming another UI surface.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 5. Visual Hierarchy Needs Rebalancing\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 The primary content should be the visual focus of the application.\
Currently, the surrounding frame and background treatment have enough contrast and definition that they compete with the actual Reading Tracker content.\
The hierarchy should instead be:\
1. Reading content / books\uc0\u8232 2. Navigation and controls\u8232 3. Application background\u8232 4. Decorative atmospheric effects\u8232 5. Window chrome\
The chrome and decorative effects should not be among the first things the eye notices.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0
