\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Content spacing\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Then ensure the decorative effects derive their positioning from the same geometry rather than being independently positioned.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 7. macOS Integration\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Because this is a macOS application, the UI should feel native without simply looking like a generic macOS window.\
The ideal result is a purpose-built macOS application that respects the platform's visual conventions while maintaining its own identity.\
The current title-bar treatment feels more like the default operating-system frame has been placed around the application.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Recommendation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Explore a more integrated approach to the title bar and toolbar.\
The application should feel as though the Reading Tracker interface occupies the entire window, with macOS controls naturally embedded into that environment.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 8. Overall Design Direction\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 The strongest direction would be to simplify the visual layering rather than adding more decoration.\
The starfield is already doing significant atmospheric work. The interface doesn't need additional strong boundaries competing with it.\
A cleaner composition could be:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Unified dark surface \uc0\u8594  subtle starfield \u8594  integrated sidebar \u8594  focused content \u8594  minimal chrome\cf2 \strokec3 \
rather than:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 macOS frame \uc0\u8594  gray title bar \u8594  dark application \u8594  sidebar \u8594  bubble \u8594  starfield\cf2 \strokec3 \
The former makes the application feel like a designed product. The latter makes it feel like several visual layers stacked on top of one another.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Priority Recommendations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 High Priority\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 1. Reduce the visual weight of the title bar.\uc0\u8232 Make the window chrome blend more naturally into the application.\
2. Fix the bubble/glow alignment.\uc0\u8232 Either align it to the application's actual geometry or make it diffuse enough that its boundaries aren't perceptible.\
3. Establish a clearer surface hierarchy.\uc0\u8232 The application should read as one cohesive visual plane rather than multiple competing layers.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Medium Priority\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 4. Establish a consistent layout grid.\uc0\u8232 Use shared geometry for the sidebar, main content, window boundaries, and decorative effects.\
5. Reduce unnecessary borders and separators.\uc0\u8232 Let spacing and contrast establish hierarchy instead of relying on additional surfaces.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Lower Priority\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 6. Refine atmospheric effects.\uc0\u8232 Once the structural issues are resolved, tune the starfield and glow so they support rather than compete with the UI.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 Design Principle\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 The core issue can be summarized in one sentence:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec3 The chrome and decorative layers are competing with the application instead of disappearing into it.\cf2 \strokec3 \
The goal should be for the user to perceive one cohesive Reading Tracker environment, not a collection of a macOS window, a dark interface, a sidebar, and a floating background effect.\
The visual treatment should ultimately feel quiet, intentional, aligned, and atmospheric, allowing the books and reading experience to remain the primary focus.\
